# Every file here is a shell script that lockers fetch over the network and pipe
# straight into `sudo bash` as root. A CRLF blob committed from a Windows
# checkout makes every line of it fail with `$'\r': command not found`, halfway
# through provisioning a device, so line endings are pinned to LF on every
# platform regardless of the committer's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
